# Implementation Plan - Downloadable Application & Website Communication & Anomaly Alert Sync

Establish full two-way communication between the downloadable **FolderGuard Agent** (downloadable application) and the **SelectShans Website**. The downloadable agent will monitor user-specified folders for anomalous activities, compile a detailed **Anomalous Activity List**, share this list with the website for live internal verification, and trigger the website to automatically send instant email notifications to the user whenever anomalous behavior is detected.

---

## User Review Required

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Communication & Workflow Steps**:
> 1. **User-Specified Folder Monitoring**: The downloadable application prompts the user for a folder to monitor (with default fallback from `config.json`).
> 2. **Anomalous Activity Marking & List Creation**: The application detects anomalous behaviors (mass renames, entropy surges, rapid writes, canary file breaches), marks each occurrence, and appends it to a structured local and in-memory activity list.
> 3. **Syncing List to Website**: The activity list is automatically pushed to the website's backend server (`/api/detector/sync-activities` & `/api/detector/log`).
> 4. **Automated Website Email Trigger**: Upon detecting anomalous behavior during list creation, the downloadable app sends an urgent trigger payload to the website, which executes `send_email_safe` (Nodemailer) to email the user.
> 5. **Website Verification UI**: The website renders a real-time **Host Anomalous Activity List** widget on the Dashboard, allowing users to inspect internal filesystem activities in real time.

